12:T71e,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I calculate GPA with credit hours?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Multiply each course grade point by its credit hours, add the results and divide by the total included credit hours. The interactive calculator performs these steps automatically."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How can I calculate the GPA needed to reach a target?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Enter your current GPA, completed credits, future credits and target GPA in the target planner. It calculates the average required across the future credits and flags a result above 4.00 as unavailable on a standard 4.0 scale."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is CGPA divided by 10 and multiplied by 100 always correct?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. It is only a proportional estimate for a 10-point scale. Universities and credential evaluators may use a different institution- or country-specific method."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I convert percentage directly to a 4.0 GPA?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"You can create a rough proportional estimate, but an official decision may consider grade bands, pass marks, institution standards and individual courses. Follow the receiving institution's instructions."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does a calculated GPA prove scholarship eligibility?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. It can help you compare an academic threshold, but official eligibility and selection depend on the complete current programme rules."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does AspireCompass store my grades?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. The calculator runs in your browser and does not require an account or submission of a transcript."}}]}1:["$","main",null,{"id":"main-content","children":[[["$","script","0",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.o