1a:["$","section","Which GPA should go on a scholarship application?",{"id":"section-4","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Which GPA should go on a scholarship application?"}],[["$","p","Use the original GPA, CGPA or percentage exactly as it appears on the official transcript unless the application gives a conversion instruction. Include the scale, such as 3.42/4.00 or 8.1/10.0, so the number has context.",{"children":"Use the original GPA, CGPA or percentage exactly as it appears on the official transcript unless the application gives a conversion instruction. Include the scale, such as 3.42/4.00 or 8.1/10.0, so the number has context."}],["$","p","When a form requires a different scale, follow that programme's stated calculator or credential-evaluation route. Save a note explaining the method and do not present an AspireCompass estimate as a university-issued result.",{"children":"When a form requires a different scale, follow that programme's stated calculator or credential-evaluation route. Save a note explaining the method and do not present an AspireCompass estimate as a university-issued result."}]],["$","ul",null,{"children":[["$","li","Original result and maximum scale",{"children":"Original result and maximum scale"}],["$","li","Institution and country",{"children":"Institution and country"}],["$","li","Programme's required conversion method",{"children":"Programme's required conversion method"}],["$","li","Calculated result with method noted",{"children":"Calculated result with method noted"}],["$","li","Official evaluation where specifically requested",{"children":"Official evaluation where specifically requested"}]]}]]}]
1b:["$","section","Common calculation mistakes",{"id":"section-5","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Common calculation mistakes"}],[["$","p","A simple average of course grades is wrong when courses carry different credits. Other common errors include mixing percentage marks with grade points, omitting repeated courses without permission and rounding every row before calculating the final result.",{"children":"A simple average of course grades is wrong when courses carry different credits. Other common errors include mixing percentage marks with grade points, omitting repeated courses without permission and rounding every row before calculating the final result."}],["$","p","Keep several decimal places during the calculation and round only the final display. If your transcript already provides a cumulative result, do not replace it with a self-calculated number unless the application explicitly asks you to recalculate it.",{"children":"Keep several decimal places during the calculation and round only the final display. If your transcript already provides a cumulative result, do not replace it with a self-calculated number unless the application explicitly asks you to recalculate it."}]],"$undefined"]}]
1c:["$","section","Use GPA as one part of scholarship fit",{"id":"section-6","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Use GPA as one part of scholarship fit"}],[["$","p","A minimum GPA is normally an eligibility threshold, not a prediction of selection. Scholarships may also evaluate degree relevance, leadership, research fit, work experience, references, language evidence and the quality of programme-specific answers.",{"children":"A minimum GPA is normally an eligibility threshold, not a prediction of selection. Scholarships may also evaluate degree relevance, leadership, research fit, work experience, references, language evidence and the quality of programme-specific answers."}],["$","p","After checking the academic threshold, use the scholarship finder to narrow programmes by degree level, destination and funding. Then verify the current criteria on the programme owner's website.",{"children":"After checking the academic threshold, use the scholarship finder to narrow programmes by degree level, destination and funding. Then verify the current criteria on the programme owner's website."}]],"$undefined"]}]
